// A module body must see the globals declared before it -- a constant, a
// variable, anything. It could not: csp_lookup_decl started the search at the
// module's own decl, so everything above was unreachable.
//
// And a member may still SHADOW a global of the same name, which is what makes
// the fix safe: adding a global later must not break a module that happens to
// use that name.
#constant K = 7
#variable G = 42

#module M
  #variable V = 0
  #variable W = 0
  V = K ? 1        // global constant, seen from inside the body
  W = G ? 1        // global variable
#end

#module S
  #variable K = 99   // shadows the global K
  #variable V = 0
  V = K ? 1          // must pick the local one
#end

#M m1
#M m2
#S s1
